re: local parks as money makers: the ones around here charge a limited fee
for camping and they book solid. If they could charge a variable fee based
on season and features, there'd be money to be made. Right now, many sites
are troubled by disputes, as dirt bikers fight with hikers, nude bathers
fight with the conservative, horseback riders fight with bicyclists, etc,
over what activities are allowed at what sites. I could imagine that, say,
taking a couple of parks and making them into dirt bike paradise, building
nudist camps near some parks and Christian or Moslem family camps near
others, would make some more money. And, there's enough park space so that
access for all would still be available, there's probably much less of a 
market for luxury camping (on the theory that the best stuff mostly already
 *is* limited to the wealthy)


